    "updated_at": "2026-08-18T13:13:10Z",
    "body": "Final review notes before merge:\n\n- CI is green for all three jobs: frontend lint + production build, backend context/JPA test on PostgreSQL 17, and Playwright Maven tests.\n- The frontend build transformed 67 modules and completed successfully after the History extraction and shared-select/API changes.\n- The CI setup exposed an existing schema-management debt: a completely empty database cannot replay Flyway from V1 because the migration chain assumes Hibernate-created base tables already exist. This PR intentionally does not invent a risky historical baseline. Backend CI therefore verifies mappings/context on an isolated Hibernate `create-drop` schema with Flyway disabled.\n- Recommended separate follow-up: create and verify a true Flyway baseline from the actual production schema, then move toward `ddl-auto: validate`.\n- Large real-action Playwright classes (offer/negotiation/filter executors) were audited structurally but deliberately not mechanically split in this PR because current tests are too sparse to justify that regression risk.\n- `npm ci` currently reports one high-severity dependency advisory. This PR does not run a blind `npm audit fix`; that should be identified and upgraded deliberately in a separate dependency change.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
